@BullishWiener I'm happy $GOOGL is being more aggressive with supply procurement like $NVDA was.

They've been way too complacent and let others bottleneck their own supply chain. 

CSPs and hyperscalers will be in a rude awakening if they're hoping for Chinese memory to save them.

@ThematicTrader How is this not valuable? Look at this.

"Industry observers say foldable phone production is ramping up faster than expected, shortening the period during which initial premiums can hold and increasing the risk of losses for speculative dealers who have taken on excessive inventory."

Market trends and inventory conditions like these are extremely important to an analyst like me.

@Global_hawk_eye I do have AVGO and MU in my portfolio. But I also have others outside the AI trade.

This is why I continue to preach to be balanced during this current market regime. 

We actually ended up positive, while everyone was panicking yesterday.

@war_346887 Current entry price on my end for $MU during our mid-September rebalance is at $939.93 fill price.

Our next rebalance for our portfolio is in December - with micro-adjustments along the way.

Remember, individual stocks do not matter. It's about the entire portfolio, each individual stock plays a key role in its make-up. Think like a sports team - you have your superstars, role players, energy off the bench, etc. Don't separate, make it cohesive in your goal.
